<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">

<div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Professional suspended ceiling installation for offices, retail, and commercial spaces across Edinburgh. Mineral fibre, metal, and acoustic tile options with integrated lighting and Scottish Building Standards compliance. 12-month guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Suspended Ceiling Services</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Suspended ceilings are one of the most effective ways to modernise a commercial interior. At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we install high-quality suspended ceiling systems that conceal ductwork, wiring, and plumbing while improving acoustics and lighting distribution across Edinburgh's diverse property portfolio.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh's commercial property sector — from office spaces on St Andrew Square and North Bridge to retail units on Princes Street and George Street, healthcare facilities across NHS Lothian, and education buildings throughout the city — demands ceiling systems that are durable, compliant, and visually clean. We supply and install ceiling systems from industry-leading manufacturers including Armstrong, Rockfon, and Ecophon, all fitted to Scottish Building Standards Part B fire safety and Part T ventilation requirements.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Mineral fibre ceiling tiles (standard and acoustic grades)</li>
  <li>Metal ceiling tiles (perforated and plain finishes)</li>
  <li>Plasterboard suspended ceilings</li>
  <li>Fire-rated ceiling systems (30–120 minutes)</li>
  <li>Moisture-resistant tiles for kitchens, bathrooms, and pool areas</li>
  <li>Integrated lighting and air vent cutouts</li>
  <li>Emergency lighting and smoke detector integration</li>
  <li>Easy-access ceiling tiles for MEP services maintenance</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Install a Suspended Ceiling?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Hide unsightly services:</strong> Suspended ceilings create a clean visual plane that conceals electrical cables, ductwork, pipes, and structural elements — essential in Edinburgh's older buildings where services are exposed.</li>
  <li><strong>Improve acoustics:</strong> Acoustic ceiling tiles absorb sound and significantly reduce noise levels in open-plan offices, meeting rooms, call centres, and hospitality venues across Edinburgh.</li>
  <li><strong>Enhance lighting:</strong> Integrated LED panels and downlights create even light distribution, eliminating dark spots and reducing energy costs — important for Edinburgh's growing ESG-driven commercial market.</li>
  <li><strong>Easy maintenance access:</strong> Individual ceiling tiles can be removed to access building services for maintenance and repairs without damaging the ceiling surface.</li>
  <li><strong>Fire safety:</strong> Fire-rated ceiling tiles and grid systems slow the spread of fire through ceiling voids and meet Scottish Building Standards Part B requirements for commercial and public buildings.</li>
  <li><strong>Quick installation:</strong> Suspended ceilings install faster than solid ceilings with minimal disruption to your Edinburgh business operations or residential property.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials & Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use high-quality ceiling systems and tiles from trusted manufacturers to ensure durability, compliance, and a professional finish across all Edinburgh projects.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Armstrong suspended ceiling grid systems (24mm and 15mm profile options)</li>
  <li>Rockfon mineral fibre ceiling tiles (NRC ratings up to 0.95)</li>
  <li>Ecophon acoustic ceiling solutions for demanding acoustic environments</li>
  <li>British Gypsum ceiling tiles (standard, acoustic, and moisture-resistant)</li>
  <li>Metal ceiling tiles (perforated, plain, and powder-coated finishes)</li>
  <li>Fire-rated tiles and grid components for Part B compliance</li>
  <li>LED panel lights and recessed downlight integration</li>
  <li>Air conditioning vent cutouts and diffusers</li>
  <li>Emergency lighting and smoke detector integration</li>
  <li>Perimeter trim and edge finishing</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications & Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our suspended ceiling services are suitable for a wide range of commercial and public buildings across Edinburgh.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Open-plan offices and co-working spaces in the New Town, Stockbridge, and St Andrew Square</li>
  <li>Retail stores and shopping centres on Princes Street, St James Centre, and Fort Kinnaird</li>
  <li>Healthcare facilities and care homes across NHS Lothian and private clinics</li>
  <li>Schools, colleges, and universities including Edinburgh Napier and Heriot-Watt campuses</li>
  <li>Warehouse and industrial unit offices in Leith, Portobello, and the Edinburgh Enterprise Zone</li>
  <li>Call centres and customer service hubs across the city</li>
  <li>Leisure centres and community buildings in the Lothians</li>
  <li>Hotels and hospitality venues in the Old Town, West End, and Leith Waterfront</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">How It Works</h2>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Free Quote:</strong> Call or fill in our form. We will survey your space and recommend the best ceiling system for your needs, including tile type, grid layout, and lighting integration.</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Plan:</strong> We confirm tile type, grid layout, lighting integration, and timeline. Everything is agreed upfront with no hidden extras, including Scottish Building Standards compliance documentation.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional Installation:</strong> Our experienced team installs the grid framework, fits the ceiling tiles, and integrates lighting and ventilation as required. We work cleanly and efficiently to minimise disruption.</li>
  <li><strong>Quality Check & Handover:</strong> We inspect every tile, test lighting and services, and leave your space looking professional and modern with full compliance documentation.</li>
</ol>

